    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d201">

                <pb facs="0490" n="394" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg394"/>

                <head>No. 180.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-07-12"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 12, 1879</date>.
                        (Received August 6.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 26.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Everything that I can learn from various
                    influential quarters here confirms the impression made upon me, * * * that
                    Germany will not sell any more silver, but that she will make reissues. I find
                    this to be the opinion of influential members of the German Parliament with whom
                    I have recently conversed, an opinion not born especially of hope, since it is
                    shared by many who are most opposed to the policy.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>AND. D. WHITE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
